    {
      "id": "claim_bbe716e4b1f74e53921f66b43a0cca70",
      "statement": "The realm-setup walkthrough's example KeycloakRealmImport protocolMappers list (groups, email, name, audience) omits any AWS session-tags mapper for the https://aws.amazon.com/tags claim that the README's OIDC identity requirements, the shared-iam module's aws:RequestTag/uuid and aws:RequestTag/roles trust conditions, and the regional ECS Exec ABAC policy all depend on, so a realm built exactly from this example issues tokens with no principal session tags and cannot satisfy UUID-allowlist, group-enforcement, or ECS Exec resource-tag conditions even though Lambda-side investigation creation may still succeed via its preferred_username fallback.",
